From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:35:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plugin: propagate TTLM backend failures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The advertised TTLM callback returns DONE to tell the AP MLD layer to
mirror the requested frequency bands into every TIDLinkMap instance. The
hostapd helper reports command rejection as an error, but the plugin
discards it and returns DONE even when hostapd logs:

    advertised_ttlm failed

This publishes a mapping that was never applied, including on backends
without ADVERTISED_TTLM support. A zero link map also incorrectly
reports DONE without sending a command.

Gate TTLM configuration on the existing ttlm_enable keyword probe,
returning NOT_IMPLEMENTED for unsupported or unknown backends. Propagate
command errors and translate only hostapd's OK into DONE so successful
commands still reach the mirror. Reject a zero map instead of claiming
completion. Failed set and clear requests keep the last applied mapping;
configuration requests remain stored by the existing change callback.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c
index d51747d1a895..d309f35a1da2 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_vap.c
@@ -770,6 +770,10 @@ swl_rc_ne wifiGen_vap_ttlm_config(T_AccessPoint* pAP, wld_tidLinkMap_m linkMap,
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pSSID, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "NULL");
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(tidLinkMapConfig, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "NULL");
 
+    ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pAP->pRadio, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "NULL radio");
+    ASSERTI_EQUALS(wld_secDmn_getCfgParamSupp(pAP->pRadio->hostapd, "ttlm_enable"),
+                   SWL_TRL_TRUE, SWL_RC_NOT_IMPLEMENTED, ME, "TTLM not supported by hostapd");
+
     if(set & DIRECT) {
         T_SSID* primarySSID = wld_mld_getPrimaryLinkSsid(pAP->pSSID->pMldLink);
         ASSERTI_NOT_NULL(primarySSID, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "NULL primarySSID");
@@ -779,18 +783,18 @@ swl_rc_ne wifiGen_vap_ttlm_config(T_AccessPoint* pAP, wld_tidLinkMap_m linkMap,
         ASSERTI_EQUALS(pAP->status, APSTI_ENABLED, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "Not enabled AP");
         ASSERTI_EQUALS(pSSID->status, RST_UP, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "Not enabled SSID");
 
-        ASSERTI_TRUE(swl_bit32_getNrSet(linkMap) >= 1, SWL_RC_DONE, ME, "Not valid linkMap");
+        ASSERTI_TRUE(swl_bit32_getNrSet(linkMap) >= 1, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "Not valid linkMap");
         SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: TTLM config set %04X %d %d",
                         pAP->alias,
                         linkMap,
                         tidLinkMapConfig->advertisedMapSwitchTime,
                         tidLinkMapConfig->advertisedExpectedDuration);
-        wld_ap_hostapd_advertised_ttlm(pAP,
+        swl_rc_ne rc = wld_ap_hostapd_advertised_ttlm(pAP,
                                        linkMap,
                                        tidLinkMapConfig->advertisedMapSwitchTime,
                                        tidLinkMapConfig->advertisedExpectedDuration,
                                        0); // LinkMapSize equals 0 means that the provided map applies for both direction
-        return SWL_RC_DONE;
+        return (rc == SWL_RC_OK) ? SWL_RC_DONE : rc;
     } else {
         setBitLongArray(pAP->fsm.FSM_BitActionArray, FSM_BW, GEN_FSM_MOD_AP);
         return SWL_RC_OK;
-- 
